[
  {
    "beat": 1,
    "flux": "A lighthouse keeper, weathered hands and oil-stained coat, kneels at the waterline of a rocky shoreline, lifting a tangled fishing net to reveal one luminous blue-green fish glowing softly. Composition centers the fish in the net’s knot, the keeper’s face partly in profile, horizon low, lighthouse tower behind. 35mm lens, shallow depth of field, gentle dawn rim light, wet rocks, mist, muted slate, silver, seafoam, faint amber. Painterly realism, cinematic still, tactile textures, quiet wonder, no text.",
    "ltx": "The keeper’s gloved fingers part the net slowly; the glowing fish pulses once, sending faint ripples through shallow seawater. Camera begins tight on the fish, then pulls back slightly as she kneels, revealing wet rocks and the distant lighthouse. Movement is slow, contemplative, with gentle drift; waves lap, mist shifts, and net fibers tremble. No music, no speech."
  },
  {
    "beat": 2,
    "flux": "A lighthouse keeper climbs a narrow spiral stone staircase, carrying a small glass jar containing the glowing fish. The jar’s soft cyan light streaks across the wet walls. Low-angle composition follows her from below, stairs curling upward into shadow, keeper’s silhouette framed by the circular stairwell. 24mm lens, deep focus, mixed light: cold stormy window light above and warm bioluminescent glow below. Palette of charcoal, slate, damp rust, luminous aqua. Cinematic realism, tense atmosphere, detailed fabric, rain-streaked glass, no text.",
    "ltx": "The keeper ascends the spiral stairs steadily, her coat and scarf swinging; the jar in her hands glows brighter with each step. Camera tracks her from behind in a slow upward tilt, then switches to a close view of the jar’s pulsing light reflecting on wet stones. Pacing builds subtly: rain streaks the window, shadows lengthen, and the handrail trembles faintly. No music, no speech."
  },
  {
    "beat": 3,
    "flux": "In the circular lamp room of a lighthouse, the glowing fish in a glass jar floats near the massive Fresnel lens, its cyan radiance spilling across brass fittings, glass prisms, and the keeper’s outstretched hand. Wide central composition symmetrical around the lens, the keeper small beneath it. 28mm lens, sharp detail, high-contrast light: cool storm light from portholes and golden-white bioluminescent flood. Palette of brass, amber, aqua, midnight blue. Hyperreal cinematic style, awe and wonder, volumetric glow, no text.",
    "ltx": "The fish’s light swells in slow pulses, flooding the lamp room; lens prisms refract expanding golden rays, and the main beam turns from white to gold. Camera starts close on the jar, pulls back through rotating light, then tilts up to the great lens as the beam intensifies. Pacing is slow at first, then accelerating gently with the storm outside; glass vibrates, brass surfaces shimmer, and the keeper’s hair lifts slightly. No music, no speech."
  },
  {
    "beat": 4,
    "flux": "A small storm-tossed ship glides between jagged dark rocks, guided by a sweeping golden lighthouse beam cutting through rain and sea spray. Low-angle composition from the deck, ship centered under the beam, rocks framing the foreground, lighthouse far behind in mist. 50mm lens, cinematic depth, dramatic chiaroscuro: gold beam against slate-green sea, charcoal sky, silver rain. Palette of gold, bronze, storm blue, wet basalt. Realistic cinematic still, heroic and serene, no text.",
    "ltx": "The golden beam sweeps across the black sea, illuminating the ship’s hull as it turns away from a rock. Camera moves smoothly with the ship from a low waterline angle, gliding through spray, then pulls wider to show the rocks parting and the lighthouse beam steady. Waves roll, rain falls, ropes creak visually, the sail flaps, and the ship tilts with swells. Pacing builds from tense to relieved. No music, no speech."
  }
]
